{"title":"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be a real-valued function defined for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that, for some positive constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8b3bbc8a56354c4a9940dfe4076f5dad29e31a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x + a) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\sqrt{f(x) - (f(x))^2}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"37\" />\nholds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>(a) Prove that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is periodic (i.e., there exists a positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb26d908eccc14446c78696ac81b7796096f518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x + b) = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />).\n</p><p>(b) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, give an example of a non-constant function with the required properties.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Since \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c0d8b1936802188854dee709b4b361158d36e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x+a) \\ge \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />\nis true for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdd0bc38caa5ed7be000fb06296b00db4fd02da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x+a)(1-f(x+a)) = \\frac{1}{4} - (f(x)-(f(x))^2) = (\\frac{1}{2}-f(x))^2\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b8de7a868b77d7f5d148e86e515659aa49cfb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x+2a) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\sqrt{(\\frac{1}{2}-f(x))^2} = \\frac{1}{2} + (f(x) - \\frac{1}{2}) = f(x)\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"43\" />\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is periodic, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c31fd0d54098261caba2b0adbdb9b6585ded425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> as a period.\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d2a273ecd239f0cc9334d3134539a0174b4df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c064796525d1d8aa9786f738ca3065a9d33965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n\\le x &lt; 2n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61976773ac77bfd41335e8766304f788b58cc0a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032f8fd5ad8bc1e5a87ffda25d250306c397cf5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+1\\le x &lt; 2n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO\" title=\"1968 IMO\">1968 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017125339\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 118/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4000/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  